// @run
// @log 5
// @warning `v != null` is always true here (v is Id)
// @hint redundant type annotation: `v` is inferred as `Id` — remove it to lean on inference
// THE INVERTED CONTROL for `alias-over-nullable-null-test.vl`'s second half. A newtype over a
// NON-nullable base admits no null, so `v != null` is a dead test: a warning and a constant,
// as `null-guard-on-non-nullable-warns.vl` pins for un-branded types (owner ruling 2026-09-26).
// The `null`-operand exemption is read twice, in `nomBinMixes` and in the equality arm; an
// ungated one would let this program reach the emitter's `bare null needs a struct-typed context`.
type Id = new i32
const v: Id = 5 as Id
if v != null { print(v) } else { print(0) }
